The vote may have been a valuable wake-up call for France if it opens the eyes of party leaders and revives the debate on how[ to] build a nation[ based] on justice and solidarity. What[ vanished] in[ April] was the comforting[ thought that although] everything was changing in the world outside[, in French] politics everything could stay the same; that two ageing parties, the Gaullists[ and the] Social[ists],[ could] share power[ as] they had done for 30 years.
