Wise received Emmy recognition again in 1982, when he[ was] nominated for directing the television movie Sk[ok]ie, starring Danny Kaye, Eli Wallach and Brian Den[ne]hy.[ The] tele[film was based on] the true story of the[ predominantly] Jewish[ community] of[ Skok]ie, Illinois, protesting[ the] right for Neo-Nazis to march in their[ town].[
]Additionally, Wise directed Richard Burton as Winston Churchill in the 1997 BBC Hall of Fame production[ The] Gathering[ Storm],[ which] aired on NBC. Wise directed Jacobi again in the[ 1996] BBC tele[film] Breaking the Code[,] about mathematician Alan Turing, as well as Albert Finney as the title character in[ 1984]’s Pope John Paul II and Robert Mitchum and[ Deborah Kerr] in the[ 1985] romantic drama Reunion at Fairborough.
